@vsm 1.2.1
@status active
// system/s5-policy/agent-policy/agent-policy-v1/agent_policy.vsm — LLM AGENT POLICY.
// S5 DECISION rmw3 2026-08-14 (translated from Spanish) (PROMOTE-AGENT-
// POLICY): 'the agent layer is a recursion of the VSM… I cannot decide
// where the LLM agent policy should live'. RESOLUTION: single home in
// system/s5-policy/agent-policy/ — the upper recursion; DO NOT fragment by
// organ (common scope); NO parallel dir. Status: ACTIVE (ratified A5
// 2026-08-15).

// ─── 0. PRINCIPLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The agent layer is VSF's upper recursion: the agents (S1/S3/S5) operate
// n02 and their organelles — gate, relocate, checks, MCP, state — are
// SHARED. Only identity differs (role, substrate, scope, channels).
// The agent policy declares that identity and its organelles, so the
// recursion has its own S5.

policy(AGENT-POLICY) {

  principle: [
    "the agents are S1/S3/S5 of the system that operates n02 — not entities
     outside the VSM; each agent is a recursion with its own S5-local",
    "SHARED organelles: gate (vsf-agent-vsl-gate), relocate
     (vsl-relocate-on-write), checks (R4.1), MCP servers, state (state.db) —
     they have a common owner/role, they are not duplicated per agent",
    "only IDENTITY differs: role, substrate, scope, channels, visibility
     contract (R13: bbh-wsl is read-only by design)",
    "implementation ALWAYS comes with a structural design proposal
     (IMPL-WITH-DESIGN-POLICY) — a plugin/hook without a design source is an
     unauditable gate (lesson: vsf-agent-vsl-gate created without a spec,
     redone via sandbox in RELOCATE-GATE-SPEC)",
    "agent policy is DOUBLE LOOP (A5): promoting design sources
     and creating new agents require explicit human approval",
  ],

  authority: [
    "S5 (rmw3): policy, design-source promotion, double loop — A5",
    "S3 (vsf-s3-planner): plan + execute [S] + supervise (φ↑ verification)",
    "S1 (vsf-s1-executor child): execution in its own repo (R13 — child repo,
     own branch, parent commits)",
    "S1 (bbh-wsl): read-only domain (R13 — bbh asymmetry is design)",
  ],

  channels: [
    "φ↑: session blocks + commits (git) — the formal channel until
     certification; afterwards coupling via NATS (vsf-ds-agent.coupling.json)",
    "φ↓: S5 directives → S3 → S1 (gate R15 enforces the inter-agent format)",
    "R15: every inter-agent exchange in VSL (communication_protocol)",
  ],

  verification: "agent-map-valid (R4.1: census .opencode/agent/*.md ≡ declared
              agents; plugins ≡ boot_manifest) — the structure does not
              depend on good will, it is enforced (PROMOTE-AGENT-POLICY)",
}
⟦ /agent_policy ⟧